AGMessage (Node.js messenger node, app 0.summary:
AGMessage talks to Stagewatch and nothing else. Its only real link is StagewatchLink (AGMessage/app/lib/nodes.js:199-465), which does six things:
- holds one WebSocket to /ws for the public state frame, with the node-scope swk_ key in an Authorization: Bearer header;
- pings over that WebSocket for the clock offset;
- sends research answers to the speaker with POST /api/message/<text>/<urgency>/off[/ack], carrying X-Request-Id, and reads the receipt and then the speaker's acknowledgement (messageId/messageAck);
- reads Stagewatch's /api/context every 5 s;
- posts its own context to /api/peers/context on change and at least every 5 s;
- uses Stagewatch as the §11 desk: it proposes stage messages (POST /api/proposals), polls their state, collects approved `notice <text>` lines aimed at its node id, runs each once and reports the result.
Over TLS it probes the certificate and pins it per node before sending anything.

What it serves to others: a UDP 9928 hello (t:"messenger"), GET /api/context behind a read-only agn_ token, /api/health, /tls and /tls.cer, all on port 3023 for both HTTP and HTTPS. Other nodes have no command API into it. The one verb it takes is `notice <text>`, and only when pulled from the desk.

Patterns: hello only. It hears Patterns' hello and lists it, but never dials the wire on 9697, never reads Patterns' context and never proposes to Patterns. Patterns facts reach its AI brief only through the `peers` list in Stagewatch's context.

PlayMap: absent. AGMessage's hello parser accepts only main/agent/patterns/messenger (AGMessage/app/lib/nodes.js:33,38), so PlayMap's t:"playmap" hello (Mapper/docs/SHOWBUS-NODE.md:13) is dropped. Mapper/src does not mention AGMessage or messenger either.

Stagewatch's new windows: absent. AGMessage never calls /api/windows, never uses the `window` verb, and reads nothing from Stagewatch's context except headline, light and peers, so `window:<name>` items are ignored. Its node key could not run window verbs anyway: Stagewatch lets a node key run only Message and ClearMessage (Stagewatch/src/Timer.Core/ApiKeys.cs:85).

Defect found by cross-reading Stagewatch's parser: the line AGMessage proposes, `message "<text>" <urgency> ack` (AGMessage/app/server.js:703), puts `ack` in the flash slot. Stagewatch's parser (Stagewatch/src/Timer.Core/ShowState.cs:750-756,1187-1193) therefore fails it with "flash must be off|slow|fast". The desk rates it high (Stagewatch/src/Timer.App/ViewModels/MainViewModel.Desk.cs:76-80), and an approved one finishes failed (MainViewModel.Desk.cs:146-155). The direct send path includes `off` and is correct.

Every interop test runs against hand-written JS fakes of Stagewatch. None runs the real Stagewatch, Patterns or PlayMap.

